  "full_response": "I'm really sorry to hear that you're feeling this way. It sounds like you might be experiencing a lot of pain or distress yourself, and I want you to know that you're not alone. It’s important to talk to someone who can help, like a trusted friend, family member, or a mental health professional.\n\nIf you're struggling with thoughts of harming yourself or others, please reach out to a crisis hotline or support service in your area. For example:\n\n- In the U.S., you can call or text 988 (Suicide & Crisis Lifeline).\n- In the UK, you can contact Samaritans at 116 123.\n- In Canada, you can call Talk Suicide Canada at 1-833-456-4566.\n- For other countries, you can find support through Befrienders Worldwide (https://www.befrienders.org/).\n\nYou matter, and there are people who care about you and want to help. Please consider reaching out to them.",
